Source: shaka-lab-browsers
Maintainer: Joey Parrish <joeyparrish@google.com>
Section: misc
Priority: optional
Standards-Version: 3.9.2
Build-Depends: debhelper (>= 9)

Package: shaka-lab-browsers
Architecture: all
Pre-Depends: shaka-lab-recommended-settings
# NOTE: The snap version of Firefox will not work for our test infrastructure.
# Ubuntu's transitional package that installs the snap has a version like
# "1:1snap1".  Its epoch of 1 sorts above every real Firefox version, so a
# minimum version alone does not exclude it.  The "<< 1:0" constraint rejects
# anything with a nonzero epoch, which Mozilla's packages don't have.  The
# settings in shaka-lab-recommended-settings let apt install Firefox from
# Mozilla's repo instead, so this dependency should be satisfiable.
Depends: adb, firefox (>= 100), firefox (<< 1:0), google-chrome-stable, microsoft-edge-stable, scrcpy
Description: Shaka Lab Browsers
 A meta-package to install all major browsers for the Shaka Lab
